From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a VMware card with 3D draws on the GPU

Entry 176 of the software rendering list ("VMware is buggy on Linux",
crbug 1327939) turned off the GPU on every VMware card, vendor 0x15ad.
Domicile is the whole desktop, so that put every window on the CPU in a
VMware guest with 3D on, where GNOME draws on the same card through
Mesa's SVGA3D driver. A reporter's VMware guest ran Domicile on the GPU
with the list ignored.

The entry is gone. Entry 50 still turns off VMware renderers older than
Mesa 9.2.1, and a VMware guest with 3D off has no GL to draw with.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 gpu/config/software_rendering_list.json | 12 ------------
 1 file changed, 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gpu/config/software_rendering_list.json b/gpu/config/software_rendering_list.json
index 4361199..5c90f0a 100644
--- a/gpu/config/software_rendering_list.json
+++ b/gpu/config/software_rendering_list.json
@@ -1347,18 +1347,6 @@
         "accelerated_video_encode"
       ]
     },
-    {
-      "id": 176,
-      "description": "VMware is buggy on Linux",
-      "cr_bugs": [1327939],
-      "os": {
-        "type": "linux"
-      },
-      "vendor_id": "0x15ad",
-      "features": [
-        "all"
-      ]
-    },
     {
       "id": 178,
       "description": "Intel IronLake only shows black in hardware decoded H264 [b/202962575, b/233244020]",
